{
  "_note": "LIP-4 Micro-Core replay vectors (2026-10-28, libraries 0.4.14): the idempotency claim under authority replacement and key reuse (LIP-4 section 2 step 3 and step 6; MCP extension draft v0.4 sections 4.1, 5.6). Each vector is a sequence of steps against one fresh idempotency cache (claim / lookup / complete / mark_indeterminate / release / abandon, as in both reference caches) and the envelope check (check_invocation / checkInvocation, with enforce_magnitude false for the disclosure check of a replay). A scope is [tenant, agent did] or a bare agent did (no tenant); an identity is the signed @method, @target-uri and content-digest lines of a verified signature base, named here for readability. These vectors are stateful, so they are an extra set for servers that keep claims, not part of the ten CONFORMANCE checks. Written after two independent reviews reproduced three faults in 0.4.13: a retry after a cap cut was refused by the cap before the stored result was found; one key reused for a different request, or by another tool sharing the cache, replayed the first result; and a second principal with the same agent key replayed the first principal's execution. Both reference test suites load this file. Second pass (same day, after a third review): a scope may also be [audience, tenant, agent did]; a claim records the tenant that reserved it, and the same agent key and key under another tenant is tenant_mismatch (refused, neither replayed nor run again); a row stored without an identity fails closed against a lookup that carries one; complete() needs a reservation and never overwrites a completed claim.",
